# What a creature's Hit Dice are levels in. A stat block prints
# 'HP 94 (9d10 + 45)', and those nine d10s are what make a Troll
# a monster rather than a species carrying a Troll's ability
# scores. One class per die size, because a single class cannot
# be a d4 and a d20 at once. That the die follows the size is
# measured from all 331 stat blocks rather than quoted: the SRD
# says only that "Hit Point Dice are provided" (p.255).

CLASS:Monster Hit Die d4	HD:4	TYPE:Monster	MAXLEVEL:50	FACT:ClassType|Monster	VISIBLE:NO
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d4	STARTSKILLPTS:0	MODTOSKILLS:NO
1:REPEATLEVEL:1	DONOTADD:SKILLPOINTS
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d6	HD:6	TYPE:Monster	MAXLEVEL:50	FACT:ClassType|Monster	VISIBLE:NO
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d6	STARTSKILLPTS:0	MODTOSKILLS:NO
1:REPEATLEVEL:1	DONOTADD:SKILLPOINTS
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d8	HD:8	TYPE:Monster	MAXLEVEL:50	FACT:ClassType|Monster	VISIBLE:NO
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d8	STARTSKILLPTS:0	MODTOSKILLS:NO
1:REPEATLEVEL:1	DONOTADD:SKILLPOINTS
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d10	HD:10	TYPE:Monster	MAXLEVEL:50	FACT:ClassType|Monster	VISIBLE:NO
CLASS:Monster Hit Die d10	STARTSKILLPTS:0	MODTOSKILLS:NO
1:REPEATLEVEL:1	DONOTADD:SKILLPOINTS
